 "findings": [
  "Gimbal (item 2): commanded neutral in the whole window (sim6 FSW: attitude loop inactive without thrust, command returned to 0 through the shaping chain; |command| < 1e-80 deg); the engine angle stays within 0.056 deg of neutral (hose spring and base excitation only), so body axes = engine axes for the angles below.",
  "No purge (A1|ref), hose station: theta at RELIGHT p50/p95/p99/max 0.11/0.45/0.63/0.75 deg; 10/500 runs above 0.6 deg, 0 above 1 deg. Over the 10 s before RELIGHT (time-pooled) 0.11/0.52/1.61/8.41 deg; share of time above 0.6 / 1 / 2 / 4 deg: 0.0384 / 0.0209 / 0.0057 / 0.0009.",
  "The large angles of the 10 s window are the drogue-deployment swing: the per-run maximum (p50/p95/p99/max 0.92/3.83/7.12/8.41 deg) occurs p50 3.2 s after the deployment, i.e. at the start of the window for the runs whose descent is short. Over the last 5 s the per-run maximum is 0.30/0.78/0.96/1.30 deg and the share of time above 0.6 deg is 0.0038.",
  "Azimuth without purge: no preferred direction (time share of theta > 0.6 deg per 45-deg sector, W10: 0 0.13, 45 0.10, 90 0.12, 135 0.15, 180 0.13, 225 0.10, 270 0.12, 315 0.16); Mechanical's worst direction (az 45 deg sector) holds 0.10 of it.",
  "Forced purge with a lateral vent (A1|P25: 2.1 N reaction toward body az 0 deg at the pivot height, ASSUMED): theta at RELIGHT 1.18/1.46/1.63/1.85 deg, all 500 runs above 0.6 deg (465 above 1 deg, 0 above 2 deg), azimuth in the jet-reaction sector (sector 0: 0.984 of the runs); during the purge (time-pooled) 1.18/1.42/1.59/2.57 deg. The vent reaction tilts the specific force by about F_jet / (m g) = 0.8 deg toward the reaction azimuth and the drogue restoring moment adds about 0.3 deg. With a balanced or axial vent (A1|P25_nojet) theta at RELIGHT is 0.12/0.43/0.63/0.72 deg (as without purge). The vent direction is therefore a design input for the hump volume (Mechanical: per-azimuth pockets; Combustion: purge sizing).",
  "Station dependence (theta at RELIGHT p95 / max, no purge): seat 0.29 / 0.55, hose 0.45 / 0.75, mv 0.65 / 1.16, pivot 0.72 / 1.31, cg 1.24 / 2.34, imu_meas 3.40 / 6.36 deg. A change of the nose-drogue force rotates the vehicle about a centre of percussion about 0.22 m below the CG, near the engine, so the engine-end stations see the smallest lateral specific force; the hose station height is ASSUMED.",
  "Measured (IMU) vector: the IMU is 0.48 m above the CG, so the raw measured angle is larger than at the hose (RELIGHT p50/p95/p99/max 0.89/3.40/5.09/6.36 deg); a 1 s trailing mean gives 0.19/0.71/0.95/1.25 deg. The physical angle for the line contents is the hose-station value.",
  "Specific-force magnitude at the hose: 10 s window p1/p5/p50 0.64/0.81/0.99 g (lowest values at the start of the window, drogue build-up); at RELIGHT 0.94-1.14 g.",
  "Mean wind < 6 m/s (proposed launch criterion, 364 runs): theta at RELIGHT 0.09/0.33/0.46/0.73 deg (no purge) and 1.16/1.37/1.55/1.63 deg (P25).",
  "Conditional hump screen (coordinator table, worst direction applied to every azimuth, humps ASSUMED additive to the 13.53 cm3 trap; allowance 5.33 cm3 reached at 2.42 deg): at RELIGHT no run exceeds it (no purge: hump max 0.73 cm3; P25: max 3.87 cm3). This screen is conservative on direction and NOT conservative on the drogue model (next item).",
  "Model limit that governs: the 6-DOF drogue is a quasi-steady massless canopy at the nose tip (no canopy pendulum oscillation, riser elasticity, swivel friction or inflation). A real canopy oscillates and its swing adds directly to theta; the values above are a lower-fidelity baseline until drop-test or literature data for the chosen canopy are folded in (HYPOTHESIS to refute: theta at the hose stays below 0.6 deg in the last 5 s of a real drogue descent)."
 ]
